noah: Heads-up: PR #5234 updates the 'Rate limits & Quotas' guide. We need a short worked example that shows how tiered pricing affects overage alerts and billing estimates (keep it one small code snippet + one sentence). cc @ariel @samir
ariel: I can write the snippet. Prefer JS since it's used across the site. Want it to show 3-tier mapping and a simple cost calc for minutes over allowance.
samir: Also call out that monitoring alerts are based on percent_of_daily and that burst credits are excluded until consumed. Keep the language customer-facing and concise.
ariel: Draft snippet (will put in PR):```js
// compute overage estimate for minutes over allowance
const tiers = {starter: {per_day:1000, price_per_token:0.0005}, pro: {per_day:10000, price_per_token:0.0004}};
function overageCost(tierName, extraTokens){
  const tier = tiers[tierName];
  return (extraTokens * tier.price_per_token).toFixed(2);
}
// example: 200 extra tokens on pro =>
console.log(overageCost('pro', 200)) // "0.08"
```
noah: Nice. Add one-line migration note: "Legacy meter header users: map old header to X-Redwood-Usage-Tier and recompute per_day allowances."
samir: Add UX note: percentages shown in alerts are rounded to whole numbers; enforcement uses integer token math. Also add a link to /docs/usage-alerts for the alerting example.
dariel: (typo, ignore)
docs-bot: Reminder: run l10n-check before merging.
noah: Action items: ariel add snippet + 1-line migration callout; samir add alert rounding sentence & link; I'll merge after docs-bot passes. Thanks! :rocket:
